<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>Account help | TLMPS</title>
    <style>
      body{margin:0;min-height:100vh;display:grid;place-items:center;padding:20px;background:#f4f0fa;font:15px 'Segoe UI',sans-serif;color:#1e293b}
      .card{width:min(440px,100%);padding:32px;background:#fff;border-radius:18px;box-shadow:0 15px 40px #3b1c5622;text-align:center}
      .logo{width:76px;height:76px;object-fit:contain}
      h1{color:#3b1c56}
      .notice{padding:14px;margin:18px 0;border-radius:9px;background:#f8f5fc;text-align:left;line-height:1.55}
      a{color:#5c2d91;font-weight:700}
      .back{display:inline-block;margin-top:12px;padding:11px 16px;border-radius:9px;background:#3b1c56;color:#fff;text-decoration:none}
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="card">
      <img class="logo" src="/img/tlmps_llogo_compressed_no_bg.png" alt="TLMPS logo">
      <h1>Need help signing in?</h1>
      <div class="notice">
        <p>For now, password resets are handled by the school office. Please contact the office with the student's admission number. A staff member must verify the parent or guardian using the school's normal process before changing the password.</p>
        <p>A phone number or admission number by itself is not enough to authorize a reset. Staff will update the student's account securely through Supabase and give the new password privately to the verified parent or guardian.</p>
      </div>
      <p>If you have forgotten the admission number, the school office can help after verifying the parent or guardian.</p>
      <a class="back" href="/login">Back to student login</a>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
